{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And on the seventh day you shall rest.</b> Also in the seventh year you shall not uproot the Sabbath of Creation from its place — so that you not say, since the entire year is called Sabbath, you need not observe the Sabbath of Creation in it (ibid.)." "<b>That your ox and your donkey may rest.</b> Give it נִיחַ — to permit it to graze and eat grasses from the ground. Or is it not so, but rather you pen it inside the house? You would say: this is not נִיחַ but distress." "<b>The son of your maidservant.</b> The verse speaks of an uncircumcised slave." "<b>And the stranger.</b> A resident alien."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:07.258063565Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}